{/* What the settings pages share besides their rows: the live region the script says Saved in
     (scripts/autosave.ts). What needs the owner, a failure with Retry or a removal with Undo, comes up
     in the app's Toast, which speaks for itself. data-autosave marks a page that saves itself: the
     root keeps room for a toast under its last control (rootState.ts), and a change lost on another
     page is left to it (managePageSave.ts). Inert until the page's script mounts. */}
<p class="sr-only" role="status" data-live data-autosave></p>
